repository-code: 'https://github.com/snomed-rust/snomed-rust'
url: 'https://snomed-rust.github.io/'
abstract: >-
  A local-first Rust workspace for working with SNOMED CT, the international
  clinical terminology used in electronic health records. It parses official
  RF2 release files, validates SCTIDs, builds an in-memory snapshot store,
  runs hierarchy and subsumption queries, evaluates Expression Constraint
  Language queries, answers FHIR terminology-service operations, parses OWL
  axioms from the OWL Expression reference set, and classifies them, using
  EL-profile subsumption plus necessary normal form generation, all with zero
  external dependencies. The repository contains code only; SNOMED CT release
  content is licensed material and is never distributed here.
